Q5. Diamond Problem
class A:
    def show(self):
        print("Class A")


class B(A):
    def show(self):
        print("Class B")


class C(A):
    def show(self):
        print("Class C")


class D(B, C):
    pass


obj = D()
obj.show()

print(D.mro())
Python uses MRO (Method Resolution Order) to solve the diamond problem. Here, B is checked before C.

